+      "name": "status_response",
+      "target": "horizon_client_lib::lan::conn::native_status_response",
+      "neoforge": "none (Bukkit's ServerListPingEvent, Paper's PaperServerListPingEvent)",
+      "side": "server",
+      "cancellable": false,
+      "mod_api": {
+        "contract": "listen"
+      }
+    }
+  ],
+  "rust_summary": "a server list ping's answer, its description, player counts and sample editable, on the connection's thread (`native_status_response`).",
+  "doc_summary": "`native_status_response(address, protocol, motd, description, max_players, online, sample)` hears each status request a server answers, on the connection's own thread (Bukkit's `ServerListPingEvent`): set `description` to the text shown instead of the motd, change `max_players` and `online`, and change, add or remove the players in `sample` (empty: left out). What no mod changes is answered as before. No `Game` and no helper there. Bundles need \"hooks\": @API:status_response@.",
+  "comments": ["crates/horizon-client/src/lan/conn.rs"]
